<article>
    <h1>{$selectedSection}</h1>
    <p>When the dependency of a physical quantity is established via some function {`\\(y = f(x)\\)`}, interesting things happen when {`\\(y\\)`} is maximum or minimum for any value of {`\\(x\\)`}. We can study these <em>extremal</em> points using the derivative of the function.</p>
    <p><strong>At an extremal point, the tangent to the curve is zero, i.e. the derivative is zero.</strong> {`\\[\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0\\]`} </p>
